% What lesson 2's five-statement pointer analysis should say.
% A fact must be derived; `:- fact.` must never be, and may use variables.
%
%   python3 diagnose.py programs/points-to.dl --expect programs/points-to.expect
%   python3 mutation.py programs/points-to.dl --expect programs/points-to.expect

pt(v3, h1).                      % v3 = v1
hpt(h1, h2).                     % *v3 = v2
pt(v4, h2).                      % v4 = *v3
:- pt(v4, h1).
:- hpt(h1, h1).
:- hpt(h2, H).                   % nothing is stored through v2
